The cliff path, wind rising. ROSALIND leads; MORDECAI follows, holding his hat on. Two SAILORS sit on a lobster pot, mending a net.

SAILOR 1
Morning, Ros.

SAILOR 2
Is that him?

ROSALIND
That’s him.

SAILOR 1
(to MORDECAI)
You’ll be closing us, then.

MORDECAI
I’ll be looking. Looking isn’t closing.

SAILOR 2
That’s what the last one said. Then he closed the lifeboat station.

MORDECAI
I am not the last one.

SAILOR 1
No. The last one had a better hat.

They laugh. ROSALIND and MORDECAI walk on.

MORDECAI
Do they always talk to strangers like that?

ROSALIND
Only the ones they like.

MORDECAI
That was liking?

ROSALIND
(climbing)
If they didn’t like you, they’d have been polite.

The lighthouse appears above them, white against the cloud. MORDECAI stops.

MORDECAI
Oh.

ROSALIND
Mind the step. The ninth one’s loose. It has been since before I was born.
